🚽 Test case: #196 -- a pointer-typed struct/union VARIABLE (`gang Foo *pp`)
🚽 used as the base of member access now follows the pointer instead of
🚽 being rejected (superseding struct_pointer_array_field_fail.brainrot,
🚽 which documented the old clean-rejection behavior). Writes through `pp`
🚽 and through the original variable `f` must be visible from both --
🚽 proving `pp` really aliases `f`'s own blob rather than a disconnected
🚽 copy (the leak struct_pointer_array_field_fail.brainrot's own comment
🚽 describes, from before resolve_struct_access() rejected pointer-typed
🚽 base variables at all).
gang Foo {
    rizz arr[3];
};

skibidi main {
    gang Foo f;
    gang Foo *pp = &f;
    pp.arr[0] = 99;
    f.arr[1] = 5;
    yapping("%d %d %d", f.arr[0], pp.arr[1], pp.arr[0]);
}
